     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin, and the usual ceiling is about 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day. A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max labeled dose.\n- **1700 mg total per day,** divided as 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** For example, 500 mg or 1000 mg twice daily.\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
